====================================================================================
Does a b=2 grid hold structure the b=1 corners miss?
====================================================================================

  --- Heisenberg N=4 ---
      R  blk  corners  fine grid  pred err %  min b=1  min b=2
  ------------------------------------------------------------
    0.6    0       16        256       34.60        1        1
    0.6    1       16        256      141.17        1        1
    1.2    0       16        256       69.97        2        1
    1.2    1       16        256      174.95        1        1

  --- H2 ---
      R  blk  corners  fine grid  pred err %  min b=1  min b=2
  ------------------------------------------------------------
    0.6    0        4         16       35.57        1        2
    0.6    1        4         16       38.28        1        1
    1.2    0        4         16       76.17        2        2
    1.2    1        4         16       81.26        1        2

  pred err % = how badly the model fitted to the CORNERS predicts the
  points it never saw, relative to the fine grid's own spread.
  Small => the corners already determine the landscape and extra bits
  add no information. Large, or more minima at b=2, => seeding has
  something to find.
